      <command:example>
        <maml:title>-------------------------- EXAMPLE 2 --------------------------</maml:title>
        <maml:introduction>
          <maml:para>
          </maml:para>
        </maml:introduction>
        <dev:code>[Environment]::Is64BitProcess</dev:code>
        <dev:remarks>
          <maml:para>
False

PS&gt; Remove-RegKey -Hive LocalMachine -Key SOFTWARE\MyKey -ComputerName Server1 -View Registry64


Description
-----------
This command is using an elevated 32-bit instance of Windows PowerShell to remove a key
from a 64-bit registry section of a remote 64-bit server. First we verify that the current console
is a 32-bit instance by using the Is64BitProcess system environment variable. 

Connecting to the 64-bit section of the remote server registry is done using the View 
parameter.











</maml:para>
